  "schema": 1,
  "finding": "PCOA-FINAL-017",
  "operation": "RB-6 double force rebuild over the owner's real staged raw, every registered TSN dataset",
  "verified_by": "Claude, 2026-08-31",
  "method": "Each dataset's real raw is copied into a PRIVATE library root and the SHIPPED tsn_library.build_consolidated(report, force=True) runs three times, separated by more than the ZIP timestamp's 2-second resolution: `pre` with the stable-identity save turned OFF (pre-fix behaviour), then `post1` and `post2` on the shipped path. Each build's bytes are SNAPSHOTTED immediately and every read happens afterwards off the snapshots - reading the live output path between builds left a Windows handle that made the next os.replace fail, which was a harness defect, not a product one. The owner's staged library is only READ.",
  "criteria": {
    "2": "two consecutive force rebuilds -> byte-identical workbook, identical tsn_normalized_workbook_identity and tsn_artifact_identity_token",
    "3": "a rebuild that SHOULD change identity still does - covered by check_tsn_identity_determinism (changed content and changed raw bytes both move the token)",
    "4": "normalized content unchanged cell-for-cell by the fix - `pre` vs `post1` content digest over every sheet's every cell",
    "5": "the ONE-TIME invalidation is real and disclosed - `the_fix_DID_move_the_bytes_once` is true for every dataset"
  },
